<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of EU grain export/import balance.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are details of EU grain export/import commitments as of April 8 in the July-to-June 1996/97 campaign, supplied by member country officials.</p>
<p>On April 10, the EU additionally granted exports of 172,300 tonnes of soft wheat and 296,000 tonnes of barley.</p>
<p>Figures below ('000 tonnes) are based on officially communicated certificates and are subject to revision.</p>
<p>			 ---------1996/97-------  ------1995/96-----</p>
<p>			    1Jul96 to 8Apr97	 1Jul95 to  8Apr96</p>
<p>			 EXPORTS  PCT(1) IMPORTS  EXPORTS    IMPORTS</p>
<p>  Soft wheat(grain)  8,998     160     891    5,620	1,203</p>
<p>  Flour (2)	    5,141     145	12    3,552	   15</p>
<p>Food aid</p>
<p>    - grain		274	66	 -	415	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	  108	60	 -	180	    -</p>
<p>Donations</p>
<p>    - grain		  0		   -	335	    -</p>
<p>    - flour (2)	   17		   -	 85	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL SOFT WHEAT   14,538     143     903   10,187	1,218</p>
<p>  Durum (grain)	  120		 477	 17	1,054</p>
<p>  Semolina (3)	   313     824	 0	 38	    0</p>
<p>  Food aid		   1		   -	 68	    -</p>
<p> TOTAL DURUM WHEAT     434     353     477	123	1,054</p>
